<article class="env-definition" id="0AMX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AMX">Definition <span data-tag="0AMX">87.5.1</span>.</a> Let $\varphi : A \to B$ be a continuous map of linearly topologized rings. We say $\varphi $ is <em>taut</em><a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001559704" id="a0001559704-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> if for every open ideal $I \subset A$ the closure of the ideal $\varphi (I)B$ is open and these closures form a fundamental system of open ideals. </p>
</article>